WEBVTT

00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:16,420
If I'm supposed to be off dairy for my cancer, can I still eat some butter?

00:00:16,420 --> 00:00:19,280
Probably one of the most common questions we get.

00:00:19,280 --> 00:00:24,960
If I'm supposed to be off dairy for my cancer, can I still eat some butter?

00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:33,600
So, understand, when we test you, we're testing you for what we believe is a food driver to your

00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:42,560
cancer. So, if dairy comes up as a food driver to your cancer, you want to not eat dairy.

00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:51,720
But it's within balance. We're not talking about you having dairy antibodies to dairy

00:00:51,720 --> 00:00:57,040
proteins to k-seen. That's what we're talking about. We're not talking about a food sensitivity

00:00:57,040 --> 00:01:01,840
that if you eat it, you're going to have this horrible reaction and you get sick.

00:01:01,840 --> 00:01:07,080
So, what are we talking about if you eat a little butter that your cancer is going

00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:12,440
to take off and grow? Though, when it tests as a driver for your cancer, you want to cut

00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:23,400
out like 95% of that if possible. So, okay, where would I be getting more growth factors

